## MONGODB INDEXES TO CREATE

```python
# Run once at startup in lifespan
async def create_indexes(db):
    # Products — most queried collection
    await db.products.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("status", 1), ("created_at", -1)])
    await db.products.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("slug", 1)], unique=True)
    await db.products.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("category_id", 1)])
    await db.products.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("flags.is_featured", 1)])
    await db.products.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("stock", 1)])  # low stock queries

    # Orders
    await db.orders.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("created_at", -1)])
    await db.orders.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("user_id", 1)])
    await db.orders.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("order_number", 1)], unique=True)
    await db.orders.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("fulfillment.status", 1)])

    # Users
    await db.users.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("email", 1)], unique=True)

    # OTPs — TTL index auto-deletes expired docs
    await db.otps.create_index("expires_at", expireAfterSeconds=0)

    # Analytics events — time-series style
    await db.analytics_events.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("event", 1), ("created_at", -1)])

    # Coupons
    await db.coupons.create_index([("tenant_id", 1), ("code", 1)], unique=True)
```

---

## COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID

- ❌ Never query without `tenant_id` on per-tenant collections
- ❌ Never store decrypted secrets in logs or responses
- ❌ Never block the event loop — all DB calls must be `await`
- ❌ Never trust client-supplied prices in checkout — always re-fetch from DB
- ❌ Never skip Razorpay signature verification before creating an order
- ❌ Never use synchronous `requests` — use `httpx.AsyncClient`
- ❌ Never return MongoDB `_id` as raw ObjectId — serialize to string in response models
- ❌ Never put per-tenant secret API calls in saas routes (wrong layer)
- ❌ Don't cache tenant configs longer than 5 min — settings changes must propagate

---

## ERROR RESPONSE FORMAT

All errors return:
```json
{
  "error": "MACHINE_READABLE_CODE",
  "message": "Human readable description",
  "details": {}
}
```

Common error codes defined in `core/exceptions.py`:
- `TENANT_NOT_FOUND` `TENANT_INACTIVE`
- `USER_NOT_FOUND` `WRONG_PASSWORD` `EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED`
- `OTP_EXPIRED` `OTP_INVALID` `OTP_MAX_ATTEMPTS`
- `PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND` `OUT_OF_STOCK`
- `COUPON_NOT_FOUND` `COUPON_EXPIRED` `COUPON_USED_UP` `MIN_ORDER_NOT_MET`
- `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` `PAYMENT_VERIFICATION_FAILED`
- `UNAUTHORIZED` `FORBIDDEN`
